1
00:00:01,508 --> 00:00:04,678
[Taiki] <i>It's Chinatsu and... Haryu?</i>

2
00:00:07,389 --> 00:00:08,348
[Taiki groans]

3
00:00:08,432 --> 00:00:10,934
You know what,
I'm sure that they're just friends!

4
00:00:11,018 --> 00:00:13,311
Like, look at us!
We're walking together, too!

5
00:00:13,895 --> 00:00:15,522
Yeah, that makes sense!

6
00:00:15,605 --> 00:00:17,816
Two people
walking together is normal, right?

7
00:00:17,899 --> 00:00:19,317
Totally.

8
00:00:19,401 --> 00:00:22,571
[Taiki] Yeah, totally... normal.

9
00:00:22,654 --> 00:00:24,573
[inaudible]

10
00:00:24,656 --> 00:00:26,158
What the...

11
00:00:26,241 --> 00:00:28,827
- Both of them are seeded teams.
- Here's what I know.

12
00:00:29,828 --> 00:00:32,330
It sounds like Haryu and Chinatsu
are in the same class,

13
00:00:32,414 --> 00:00:33,832
and they sit next to each other.

14
00:00:33,915 --> 00:00:36,835
What's more, they were
both elected class representatives.

15
00:00:36,918 --> 00:00:39,671
- I don't know what those mean.
- 'Cause you're from different worlds.

16
00:00:39,755 --> 00:00:41,214
SAME CLASS, SIT TOGETHER, BOTH REPS

17
00:00:41,798 --> 00:00:43,258
But it's nothing to fret over.

18
00:00:43,341 --> 00:00:46,720
Chinatsu said she wanted to focus
on basketball for now, remember?

19
00:00:46,803 --> 00:00:48,472
Uh, yeah, that may be true.

20
00:00:48,555 --> 00:00:52,225
But it's not like falling in love
is just a switch you can flip off!

21
00:00:52,309 --> 00:00:54,436
I guess that's a good argument.

22
00:00:55,145 --> 00:00:57,981
Almost sounds like
he pulled that from an anime.

23
00:00:59,149 --> 00:01:01,151
[opening theme song playing]

24
00:01:02,235 --> 00:01:05,489
BLUE BOX

25
00:02:21,648 --> 00:02:27,946
BLUE BOX

26
00:02:28,613 --> 00:02:31,700
EPISODE 3
CHII

27
00:02:31,783 --> 00:02:34,244
What do you think about this year's batch?

28
00:02:34,327 --> 00:02:37,455
Well, our core's going to be
the third-years, plus Kengo Haryu.

29
00:02:38,415 --> 00:02:40,750
[assistant coach]
He's really that good, Coach?

30
00:02:40,834 --> 00:02:44,212
[Coach Yuasa] He's got the potential
to dominate on the national level.

31
00:02:44,296 --> 00:02:47,883
But I personally have high hopes
for where this first year is going.

32
00:02:47,966 --> 00:02:49,259
[grunts]

33
00:02:49,342 --> 00:02:50,468
[whistle blows]

34
00:02:52,971 --> 00:02:54,556
[Chinatsu] Sorry! I'll get it.

35
00:02:57,309 --> 00:02:58,435
[Taiki] <i>Chinatsu.</i>

36
00:03:00,186 --> 00:03:03,982
<i>Every time I see her now,
I keep flashing back to yesterday.</i>

37
00:03:05,275 --> 00:03:06,484
- Later.
- Ah, wait!

38
00:03:07,402 --> 00:03:09,487
When are you done with practice today?

39
00:03:09,571 --> 00:03:10,697
[Taiki gasps]

40
00:03:10,780 --> 00:03:12,949
It's just I forgot my keys at home,

41
00:03:13,033 --> 00:03:15,243
and, well, everyone said
they were going to be out late.

42
00:03:15,327 --> 00:03:16,912
I should be done around 7:00.

43
00:03:16,995 --> 00:03:19,539
<i>Wait! What if someone
overhears our conversation?</i>

44
00:03:19,623 --> 00:03:21,249
Practice should be over by then.

45
00:03:21,333 --> 00:03:23,376
- Okay, so then--
- Chii.

46
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:25,754
Does your team have an extra timer?

47
00:03:25,837 --> 00:03:27,047
Ours is busted.

48
00:03:27,130 --> 00:03:29,174
- [Taiki] <i>"Chii"?</i>
- [Chinatsu] I don't think we do.

49
00:03:29,257 --> 00:03:34,304
- [Haryu] <i>I figured.</i>
- [Taiki] <i>Did he just call Chinatsu "Chii"?</i>

50
00:03:35,347 --> 00:03:36,890
[Taiki running, panting]

51
00:03:38,099 --> 00:03:39,768
<i>I'm so jealous!</i>

52
00:03:39,851 --> 00:03:42,771
<i>"Chii"! That means
they gotta be insanely close!</i>

53
00:03:42,854 --> 00:03:46,900
Why can't I use
a cutesy nickname for Chinatsu?

54
00:03:47,651 --> 00:03:50,820
<i>Plus, she didn't even think twice
about him calling her that.</i>

55
00:03:50,904 --> 00:03:51,821
- Hey, Chii!
- Hi!

56
00:03:51,905 --> 00:03:54,449
{\an8}[Taiki] <i>What kind of vibe check
does a guy gotta pass with her?</i>

57
00:03:54,532 --> 00:03:56,284
{\an8}- I wanna call you "Chii."
- Request approved.

58
00:03:56,368 --> 00:03:58,703
[Taiki] <i>Is it 'cause
they're in the same grade?</i>

59
00:03:58,787 --> 00:04:00,288
<i>Or sit next to each other?</i>

60
00:04:00,372 --> 00:04:04,084
<i>Or is it some sort of bond
that exists between the elite athletes?</i>

61
00:04:06,503 --> 00:04:07,671
[groans]

62
00:04:08,713 --> 00:04:09,923
<i>This is not a good look.</i>

63
00:04:10,966 --> 00:04:13,176
<i>Trying to figure it out
won't change anything anyway.</i>

64
00:04:14,010 --> 00:04:18,682
<i>It's not as if I can just
jump to the same grade as Chinatsu.</i>

65
00:04:19,432 --> 00:04:21,935
<i>And even if she told me
I could call her Chii,</i>

66
00:04:22,018 --> 00:04:23,687
<i>I don't think I'd able to.</i>

67
00:04:24,437 --> 00:04:25,939
<i>If we weren't living together,</i>

68
00:04:26,022 --> 00:04:28,942
<i>or in a situation
where using nicknames is normal,</i>

69
00:04:29,693 --> 00:04:31,945
<i>I wouldn't even be thinking about it.</i>

70
00:04:34,489 --> 00:04:36,700
<i>Chii... Chii... Chii...</i>

71
00:04:36,783 --> 00:04:38,451
- I'm home.
- Chinatsu!

72
00:04:38,535 --> 00:04:39,953
[gasps] Something wrong?

73
00:04:40,036 --> 00:04:41,705
No, everything is fine.

74
00:04:41,788 --> 00:04:44,833
<i>I'm such a creep! I'm such a creep!</i>

75
00:04:44,916 --> 00:04:47,711
<i>What do you get if you
add pathetic and creepy? Me!</i>

76
00:04:47,794 --> 00:04:48,753
[Chinatsu sighs]

77
00:04:50,755 --> 00:04:52,757
You got home fast huh, Taiki?

78
00:04:52,841 --> 00:04:53,967
What?

79
00:04:54,551 --> 00:04:56,011
As I was leaving practice,

80
00:04:56,094 --> 00:04:59,723
the badminton team members
were only just getting to their clubroom.

81
00:04:59,806 --> 00:05:01,308
You said you'd finish at 7:00,

82
00:05:01,391 --> 00:05:03,727
but it seemed like
you guys were running late.

83
00:05:04,477 --> 00:05:06,271
[Taiki] <i>Yep, I've got it bad.</i>

84
00:05:07,731 --> 00:05:10,400
<i>When she said,
"the badminton team members,"</i>

85
00:05:10,483 --> 00:05:13,486
<i>I couldn't help but think
she really meant Haryu.</i>

86
00:05:14,362 --> 00:05:16,323
- Sorry, I'll be in my room--
- Oh, wait.

87
00:05:16,406 --> 00:05:17,240
[grunts]

88
00:05:17,324 --> 00:05:18,575
[groans]

89
00:05:19,284 --> 00:05:20,368
My bad.

90
00:05:21,202 --> 00:05:23,246
I just wanted to ask you something.

91
00:05:23,997 --> 00:05:26,249
I'm going to be embarrassed if I'm wrong.

92
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:29,002
But did you run home?

93
00:05:29,753 --> 00:05:33,006
It seemed like you were sweating,
so I thought you might've.

94
00:05:33,631 --> 00:05:36,259
Did you... get home before me just so that...

95
00:05:36,926 --> 00:05:39,471
<i>I wouldn't be waiting outside for you?</i>

96
00:05:43,016 --> 00:05:45,268
<i>- How'd she know what I was thinking?</i>
- I did wait, but...

97
00:05:45,351 --> 00:05:49,022
[Taiki] <i>Here I was worrying about
something stupid like what I call her.</i>

98
00:05:50,231 --> 00:05:53,359
<i>Knowing she was paying attention
to me makes me happy,</i>

99
00:05:53,443 --> 00:05:56,071
<i>and it feels like
the other stuff doesn't matter.</i>

100
00:05:56,154 --> 00:05:57,530
[Chinatsu] If I am right...

101
00:05:59,282 --> 00:06:00,784
it was a pretty good assist!

102
00:06:01,701 --> 00:06:02,744
[Taiki exclaims]

103
00:06:03,369 --> 00:06:05,455
That wasn't it at all!

104
00:06:05,538 --> 00:06:08,541
I just thought I'd fit some more training
into my commute!

105
00:06:09,626 --> 00:06:12,253
You know, I think I'll run a bit more now!

106
00:06:15,882 --> 00:06:19,552
[Taiki] <i>Having her move in with us
out of nowhere has me scrambled.</i>

107
00:06:19,636 --> 00:06:22,806
<i>Haryu's not someone
I can take head-on anyway.</i>

108
00:06:22,889 --> 00:06:26,810
<i>It doesn't matter who Chinatsu's with,
or what they call her...</i>

109
00:06:26,893 --> 00:06:29,395
<i>I can't let myself worry
about every little thing.</i>

110
00:06:29,479 --> 00:06:32,315
<i>Right now, I need to focus
on the club matches.</i>

111
00:06:33,691 --> 00:06:37,070
<i>But I may still get triggered
when I hear him call her "Chii."</i>

112
00:06:39,405 --> 00:06:41,825
- [umpire] In! Game, Inomata!
- [Taiki pants]

113
00:06:42,450 --> 00:06:45,286
{\an8}[Kyo] You won another one.
Everything's going to plan.

114
00:06:45,370 --> 00:06:49,791
{\an8}[Taiki] Yeah! Then again,
I've mostly played first-years so far.

115
00:06:49,874 --> 00:06:52,460
I haven't played
any of the regular members yet.

116
00:06:53,628 --> 00:06:54,546
Also...

117
00:06:54,629 --> 00:06:57,590
[Kyo] Haryu has won
every single one of his matches.

118
00:06:58,550 --> 00:06:59,968
So, what's the update?

119
00:07:00,051 --> 00:07:03,179
Did you decide what to do
about the two of them being so close?

120
00:07:03,263 --> 00:07:04,347
[Taiki] Well, about that.

121
00:07:05,140 --> 00:07:07,308
No matter what's going on between them,

122
00:07:07,392 --> 00:07:09,644
I decided to not let it affect me.

123
00:07:09,727 --> 00:07:13,106
If you're thinking about it that way,
it affected you.

124
00:07:16,192 --> 00:07:19,863
For real! It feels so weird
being an upperclassman, right?

125
00:07:20,530 --> 00:07:21,448
See, I don't care.

126
00:07:21,531 --> 00:07:23,741
Okay, then why are you turning back?

127
00:07:23,825 --> 00:07:26,369
[Chinatsu] Badminton's doing
a bracket within the club, right?

128
00:07:26,453 --> 00:07:28,830
Yup, and this guy
hasn't lost a single match.

129
00:07:28,913 --> 00:07:30,248
Yeah, so far I guess.

130
00:07:30,331 --> 00:07:31,749
Don't be so modest.

131
00:07:31,833 --> 00:07:34,836
This is where things get going.
I'm not done yet.

132
00:07:34,919 --> 00:07:37,755
- Gotcha. Well, do your best!
- Thank you.

133
00:07:38,465 --> 00:07:39,883
I don't care at all.

134
00:07:39,966 --> 00:07:42,385
[Nishida] You two seem to be
getting along lately, huh?

135
00:07:42,469 --> 00:07:45,346
You've been spending a lot of time
with Kano, haven't you?

136
00:07:45,430 --> 00:07:47,640
I mean, our seats
are right next to each other.

137
00:07:47,724 --> 00:07:49,476
- [groans]
- [Nishida] Mm-hm, is that all?

138
00:07:49,559 --> 00:07:51,519
- [Kyo] He started melting.
- [Haryu] It's nothing.

139
00:07:51,603 --> 00:07:53,146
We're both busy with our clubs.

140
00:07:53,229 --> 00:07:54,397
[Haryu] But...

141
00:07:55,315 --> 00:07:58,401
I do like girls who are
willing to go after what they want.

142
00:07:58,485 --> 00:07:59,819
[Taiki] <i>Wait. Does that mean...</i>

143
00:07:59,903 --> 00:08:01,404
[Haryu] It's not like that, bro!

144
00:08:01,988 --> 00:08:03,406
[Taiki breathes heavily]

145
00:08:04,157 --> 00:08:06,826
[Kyo] <i>Wow, talk about
worst possible timing.</i>

146
00:08:09,496 --> 00:08:11,414
[umpire] Love all. Play!

147
00:08:12,499 --> 00:08:13,541
[both grunting]

148
00:08:15,543 --> 00:08:16,920
[umpire] In. Five to one!

149
00:08:17,003 --> 00:08:19,339
Haryu's had the advantage this whole time.

150
00:08:19,422 --> 00:08:21,090
He's not leaving any openings.

151
00:08:21,174 --> 00:08:22,926
No kidding, he's like a brick wall.

152
00:08:23,718 --> 00:08:25,261
Is he doing okay?

153
00:08:25,345 --> 00:08:27,013
He's getting dominated.

154
00:08:27,096 --> 00:08:28,431
That's just how it goes.

155
00:08:28,515 --> 00:08:30,642
There's a difference
in their skill levels,

156
00:08:30,725 --> 00:08:33,436
and a second-year's
gonna have more experience.

157
00:08:33,520 --> 00:08:36,689
- [sighs] Oh, boy.
- [Kyo] <i>This is rough on him.</i>

158
00:08:37,857 --> 00:08:40,401
<i>His opponent gets along
with the girl he likes.</i>

159
00:08:40,485 --> 00:08:43,196
<i>Then there's the possibility
that Haryu likes her, too.</i>

160
00:08:43,279 --> 00:08:46,199
<i>And he's closer
to achieving Taiki's goals.</i>

161
00:08:47,158 --> 00:08:49,452
<i>Exposing the differences between them,</i>

162
00:08:49,536 --> 00:08:53,665
<i>it's like Haryu's telling Taiki to give up
on both nationals and Chinatsu.</i>

163
00:08:55,708 --> 00:08:56,543
Hm?

164
00:08:57,126 --> 00:08:58,545
[shuttlecock thudding]

165
00:08:58,628 --> 00:09:00,547
- [girl] Natsu!
- Coming!

166
00:09:04,384 --> 00:09:05,802
[umpire] In. Eleven to four!

167
00:09:05,885 --> 00:09:08,388
[boy 1] Haryu's gonna win
this one, too, huh?

168
00:09:08,471 --> 00:09:11,307
[boy 2] He's a powerhouse.
Come on, somebody beat him!

169
00:09:13,810 --> 00:09:14,936
You okay, dude?

170
00:09:15,019 --> 00:09:16,396
Have some water.

171
00:09:16,479 --> 00:09:17,564
Hey.

172
00:09:18,523 --> 00:09:20,567
I was close to winning, right?

173
00:09:21,943 --> 00:09:24,279
I wasn't in position in time.

174
00:09:24,362 --> 00:09:26,823
The second I stop paying attention,
I get behind.

175
00:09:26,906 --> 00:09:28,825
- You're doing well, though.
- Nah,

176
00:09:28,908 --> 00:09:30,827
I've had a good run of it, that's all.

177
00:09:30,910 --> 00:09:32,662
No, actually I thought...

178
00:09:32,745 --> 00:09:34,789
other things would be bothering you.

179
00:09:34,872 --> 00:09:36,708
Like what we overheard earlier.

180
00:09:38,167 --> 00:09:39,335
Yeah.

181
00:09:40,295 --> 00:09:44,591
Chinatsu's definitely one of the reasons
why I want to try harder and get better.

182
00:09:45,300 --> 00:09:47,719
But to use her as an excuse when I lose...

183
00:09:47,802 --> 00:09:49,846
that's not something I wanna do.

184
00:09:50,888 --> 00:09:54,350
And it's not like I'm playing badminton
just for her sake.

185
00:09:55,143 --> 00:09:56,519
The fact is that...

186
00:09:57,186 --> 00:09:58,855
I love badminton.

187
00:09:59,647 --> 00:10:01,858
- [boy] Taiki, ready to play?
- Okay!

188
00:10:02,609 --> 00:10:04,444
[Taiki] <i>It all may be true, but...</i>

189
00:10:04,527 --> 00:10:05,612
[gasps softly]

190
00:10:11,951 --> 00:10:13,077
[gasps]

191
00:10:17,665 --> 00:10:19,417
<i>I made up my mind.</i>

192
00:10:19,500 --> 00:10:21,586
<i>Even if it's one step, I'm taking it.</i>

193
00:10:24,922 --> 00:10:25,798
<i>One step.</i>

194
00:10:26,382 --> 00:10:28,176
Oh, that was a good receive.

195
00:10:28,259 --> 00:10:30,762
- [boy 1] Came right back though.
- [boy 2] Hang in there, Taiki!

196
00:10:30,845 --> 00:10:31,679
[Taiki] <i>One step.</i>

197
00:10:31,763 --> 00:10:32,680
[gasps]

198
00:10:32,764 --> 00:10:34,182
[boy] It got lofted.

199
00:10:36,267 --> 00:10:37,435
[Taiki grunts]

200
00:10:44,025 --> 00:10:47,737
[Kyo] That was close. You were making
a comeback in the second half.

201
00:10:47,820 --> 00:10:49,947
I think you should be proud of yourself.

202
00:10:50,698 --> 00:10:52,492
You may have lost to Haryu today,

203
00:10:52,575 --> 00:10:54,827
but considering your score,
I think you'll make the team.

204
00:10:56,245 --> 00:10:57,580
[Taiki grunts]

205
00:10:58,373 --> 00:10:59,916
You don't seem too happy.

206
00:10:59,999 --> 00:11:01,834
Well, at the end of the day, I lost.

207
00:11:02,585 --> 00:11:05,755
I scored in the second half,
but it felt like sheer willpower.

208
00:11:05,838 --> 00:11:08,591
Haryu was setting the pace
for the entire match.

209
00:11:09,425 --> 00:11:10,301
{\an8}BURNABLE TRASH

210
00:11:10,385 --> 00:11:12,845
{\an8}[Taiki] I knew
that he was a strong player, but...

211
00:11:14,430 --> 00:11:16,140
it's still annoying.

212
00:11:17,183 --> 00:11:18,351
[pensive music playing]

213
00:11:18,434 --> 00:11:20,269
Straight outta the horse's mouth.

214
00:11:20,353 --> 00:11:22,105
The audacity of that little dweeb.

215
00:11:22,772 --> 00:11:24,899
If anything, I'm the one who's annoyed.

216
00:11:24,982 --> 00:11:27,235
Wait, why? You won though.

217
00:11:28,736 --> 00:11:30,154
Because in the end...

218
00:11:31,656 --> 00:11:33,741
[Nishida] Wait, now I've gotta know, man!

219
00:11:33,825 --> 00:11:35,410
Come on! Tell me!

220
00:11:36,828 --> 00:11:39,330
[Taiki] <i>Well, I knew
it wasn't going to be easy.</i>

221
00:11:39,872 --> 00:11:42,250
<i>After all, my opponent was Haryu.</i>

222
00:11:42,333 --> 00:11:44,419
<i>You look at technique, speed, power...</i>

223
00:11:44,502 --> 00:11:47,088
<i>He's got me beat in all areas of the game.</i>

224
00:11:47,171 --> 00:11:49,715
<i>I need to play
on my own terms, have a plan.</i>

225
00:11:50,383 --> 00:11:52,760
<i>Adjust my shots to my opponent,</i>

226
00:11:52,844 --> 00:11:54,846
<i>and take the openings as they come.</i>

227
00:11:55,638 --> 00:11:58,349
<i>In order to do that,
I need more experience.</i>

228
00:11:58,891 --> 00:12:00,643
<i>I haven't practiced nearly enough.</i>

229
00:12:00,726 --> 00:12:01,727
Taiki.

230
00:12:04,021 --> 00:12:05,731
- Come with me.
- Chinatsu?

231
00:12:05,815 --> 00:12:08,276
Hurry the sun's going down!
Come on, let's go!

232
00:12:08,359 --> 00:12:10,987
Uh, but... where are we going?

233
00:12:11,070 --> 00:12:12,864
- A good spot.
- Hm?

234
00:12:15,491 --> 00:12:18,411
[Taiki] Well, it certainly
is a good spot, but...

235
00:12:18,494 --> 00:12:20,371
why are we in a park?

236
00:12:20,455 --> 00:12:22,165
[Chinatsu] That would be because...

237
00:12:22,248 --> 00:12:23,416
Ta-da!

238
00:12:23,499 --> 00:12:25,418
Take a look at what I borrowed for us!

239
00:12:25,501 --> 00:12:28,921
Hm? Why did you borrow rackets, Chinatsu?

240
00:12:29,005 --> 00:12:31,549
[Chinatsu] You said
we should play sometime, right?

241
00:12:31,632 --> 00:12:34,677
[Taiki gasps] <i>She remembered I said that.</i>

242
00:12:35,386 --> 00:12:36,888
Besides, knowing you,

243
00:12:36,971 --> 00:12:39,807
I thought there was a good chance
you would want to practice more.

244
00:12:39,891 --> 00:12:43,811
You know, I usually wanna practice
the most right after a game.

245
00:12:44,353 --> 00:12:46,314
And I thought you might be the same.

246
00:12:47,023 --> 00:12:50,776
[Taiki] <i>It makes me really happy
having someone in my life</i>

247
00:12:50,860 --> 00:12:52,820
<i>who understands what I'm feeling.</i>

248
00:12:53,529 --> 00:12:54,906
[Chinatsu] Here it goes.

249
00:12:54,989 --> 00:12:56,657
[happy music playing]

250
00:12:58,868 --> 00:13:00,328
[laughs] <i>She can't hit it?</i>

251
00:13:00,411 --> 00:13:02,997
Wait, it's not like that.
I just suck at serving.

252
00:13:03,706 --> 00:13:06,167
[Taiki] Your left hand is moving too much.

253
00:13:06,250 --> 00:13:09,545
Just drop the shuttle with it.
Then swing the racket forward.

254
00:13:13,090 --> 00:13:15,927
Oh, you know what you're talking about!

255
00:13:16,010 --> 00:13:17,512
It's just one of the basics.

256
00:13:18,221 --> 00:13:21,182
[Chinatsu] Hold on, this is turning
into a practice session for me.

257
00:13:21,265 --> 00:13:22,850
Shouldn't we work swings?

258
00:13:22,934 --> 00:13:26,229
[Taiki] Don't worry about it. I got in
plenty of those during my matches!

259
00:13:26,312 --> 00:13:29,148
I saw. Your match with Haryu today.

260
00:13:30,191 --> 00:13:32,151
Erase that from your memory, please.

261
00:13:32,235 --> 00:13:33,152
Why?

262
00:13:33,236 --> 00:13:36,239
[Taiki] I mean, it was embarrassing.
I lost that match.

263
00:13:36,322 --> 00:13:38,199
[Chinatsu] What's embarrassing about it?

264
00:13:38,282 --> 00:13:40,368
You nailed that smash at the end, right?

265
00:13:40,451 --> 00:13:41,661
[Taiki] Yeah, but still...

266
00:13:42,370 --> 00:13:43,704
[Chinatsu] <i>Don't forget...</i>

267
00:13:43,788 --> 00:13:47,458
<i>at the interval of the second game,
it was eleven to four,</i>

268
00:13:47,542 --> 00:13:50,086
but by the time it got to 21 points,

269
00:13:50,169 --> 00:13:53,923
Haryu had scored ten points,
and you had scored 11, Taiki.

270
00:13:55,007 --> 00:13:58,594
Huh? Hmm, hmm. Hmm.

271
00:13:58,678 --> 00:14:00,513
Losing is still losing, though!

272
00:14:01,347 --> 00:14:04,600
I couldn't even score in the first half
because of my skill level.

273
00:14:04,684 --> 00:14:07,770
And even if I scored in the second half,
it was still a loss.

274
00:14:07,853 --> 00:14:09,272
[laughs]

275
00:14:10,606 --> 00:14:11,566
[exclaims]

276
00:14:12,108 --> 00:14:14,318
Wait. What's so funny about that?

277
00:14:14,402 --> 00:14:15,528
Sorry, sorry.

278
00:14:16,320 --> 00:14:18,781
You're not a big fan of losing,
are you, Taiki?

279
00:14:18,865 --> 00:14:21,951
[Coach Yuasa] Don't swing
with your upper body. Use your legs.

280
00:14:22,034 --> 00:14:23,077
[Taiki] Yes!

281
00:14:23,160 --> 00:14:26,289
[Chinatsu] <i>Whenever anyone calls out
an aspect of your play at practice,</i>

282
00:14:26,372 --> 00:14:28,291
<i>you work on it the whole next morning.</i>

283
00:14:29,041 --> 00:14:33,045
And in your match against Haryu,
you never gave up, right?

284
00:14:33,754 --> 00:14:35,798
You scored a lot in the second half.

285
00:14:36,883 --> 00:14:38,301
That's why it's okay.

286
00:14:40,469 --> 00:14:42,805
Taiki, you've got this!

287
00:14:44,515 --> 00:14:46,559
[Taiki] <i>Knowing how far I have to go,</i>

288
00:14:47,226 --> 00:14:50,688
<i>it can be pretty challenging
to actually believe in myself.</i>

289
00:14:52,440 --> 00:14:53,566
I'll win the next one.

290
00:14:54,734 --> 00:14:56,068
That's the spirit.

291
00:14:56,152 --> 00:14:58,946
[Taiki] <i>But having the support
of someone I like...</i>

292
00:14:59,030 --> 00:15:00,823
<i>makes it so much easier.</i>

293
00:15:04,660 --> 00:15:05,870
YUKIKO

294
00:15:06,412 --> 00:15:08,789
[Chinatsu] Oh. It's from Yukiko.

295
00:15:08,873 --> 00:15:09,957
[Taiki] My mom?

296
00:15:10,541 --> 00:15:12,710
She wants to know when we'll be back.

297
00:15:13,294 --> 00:15:14,712
{\an8}[Taiki] <i>Chii?</i>

298
00:15:15,338 --> 00:15:17,006
<i>Don't tell me Haryu...</i>

299
00:15:17,089 --> 00:15:19,091
<i>gave that to her as a present?</i>

300
00:15:20,009 --> 00:15:23,137
Oh, this?
It was a gift from a friend in my class.

301
00:15:23,763 --> 00:15:26,140
Yeah, almost everyone
in my year calls me Chii.

302
00:15:26,223 --> 00:15:27,475
[gasps softly]

303
00:15:27,558 --> 00:15:30,519
[Taiki] <i>So, it turns out
Haryu wasn't special after all.</i>

304
00:15:32,939 --> 00:15:35,608
<i>It seems Chinatsu
is friendly with everybody.</i>

305
00:15:36,233 --> 00:15:39,111
<i>I guess she isn't
interested in dating right now.</i>

306
00:15:40,488 --> 00:15:42,490
Well, should we get going?

307
00:15:42,573 --> 00:15:44,700
- You go on ahead.
- [exclaims]

308
00:15:44,784 --> 00:15:47,411
I mean, there'll be
a lot of people on the way.

309
00:15:48,120 --> 00:15:51,207
Maybe it isn't
such a big deal to you, Chinatsu,

310
00:15:51,290 --> 00:15:53,417
but going to the same house with a girl...

311
00:15:53,501 --> 00:15:55,211
would make me uncomfortable.

312
00:15:55,294 --> 00:15:56,295
[Chinatsu exclaims]

313
00:15:56,379 --> 00:15:58,756
I'm gonna be practicing my swings.

314
00:15:59,465 --> 00:16:00,883
[grunts]

315
00:16:07,223 --> 00:16:09,725
[Chinatsu] <i>Not a big deal to me?</i>

316
00:16:13,604 --> 00:16:15,481
<i>That's how it looks to him, huh?</i>

317
00:16:20,194 --> 00:16:22,113
{\an8}EIMEI PRIVATE HIGH SCHOOL

318
00:16:22,905 --> 00:16:24,615
[Taiki] <i>Wait. Why?</i>

319
00:16:25,741 --> 00:16:27,868
DOUBLES
HARYU AND INOMATA

320
00:16:28,577 --> 00:16:31,372
[Taiki] How'd I get partnered
with Haryu for doubles?

321
00:16:32,039 --> 00:16:35,626
I'd been working out how to beat him,
and now we're playing together?

322
00:16:35,710 --> 00:16:37,086
Yeah, you know what else?

323
00:16:37,169 --> 00:16:40,047
Going to nationals with your love rival
is pretty weird.

324
00:16:41,590 --> 00:16:44,635
Even if you forget the part
where I like Chinatsu, I...

325
00:16:44,719 --> 00:16:45,886
- Taiki.
- [exclaims]

326
00:16:46,512 --> 00:16:48,806
- Come on, let's get at it.
- Oh, sure thing.

327
00:16:50,266 --> 00:16:53,894
For the time being, I'll start you
on the same training regimen as me.

328
00:16:53,978 --> 00:16:55,604
[Taiki] <i>Thank goodness.</i>

329
00:16:55,688 --> 00:16:57,982
<i>It seems like
he didn't hear what I just said.</i>

330
00:16:58,065 --> 00:16:58,899
[Haryu] So...

331
00:17:00,276 --> 00:17:02,903
I couldn't help but overhear
that you like Chinatsu?

332
00:17:02,987 --> 00:17:05,156
[groans]

333
00:17:07,283 --> 00:17:08,409
[whistle blows]

334
00:17:08,492 --> 00:17:12,413
[Taiki] <i>This is the worst start
to any doubles pair I've ever had!</i>

335
00:17:14,957 --> 00:17:16,000
You're too slow!

336
00:17:16,083 --> 00:17:17,418
Fix your swing and feet!

337
00:17:17,501 --> 00:17:18,419
Gotcha!

338
00:17:18,502 --> 00:17:20,921
[boy 1] Man, Haryu's
like a drill sergeant.

339
00:17:21,005 --> 00:17:24,550
This is all after they ran,
did circuit training, and footwork, right?

340
00:17:24,633 --> 00:17:26,927
[boy 2] I'd be hurling by now
if it was me.

341
00:17:27,011 --> 00:17:28,345
[panting]

342
00:17:29,013 --> 00:17:30,931
I guess you're feeling worn out, then?

343
00:17:31,515 --> 00:17:34,894
Say the word if you're done.
Would be a bummer if you passed out.

344
00:17:34,977 --> 00:17:37,021
- Yes--
- Although, I can't say

345
00:17:37,104 --> 00:17:40,441
that I've ever seen Chii mumbling
and grumbling during practice.

346
00:17:41,192 --> 00:17:42,943
Chii's future boyfriend...

347
00:17:43,027 --> 00:17:45,946
He must be a pretty cool guy
to go out with her.

348
00:17:47,323 --> 00:17:49,575
[Taiki] All right, what are we doing next?

349
00:17:49,658 --> 00:17:51,660
[Haryu] Five sets of two-minute rallies.

350
00:17:53,037 --> 00:17:54,705
[school bell rings]

351
00:17:56,540 --> 00:17:58,125
[groans softly]

352
00:17:59,043 --> 00:18:01,796
He looks like a mushroom
that grew out of the desk.

353
00:18:01,879 --> 00:18:03,672
And not a nutritious one either.

354
00:18:03,756 --> 00:18:05,216
Stop talking.

355
00:18:06,217 --> 00:18:09,220
<i>I've been getting put through the ringer
over the last week.</i>

356
00:18:09,303 --> 00:18:11,222
<i>The training has kicked my butt.</i>

357
00:18:11,305 --> 00:18:15,434
At this point, the classroom is
the only place I have left to chill out.

358
00:18:15,518 --> 00:18:17,478
- Not home?
- [Kyo] Yeah, it took me by surprise.

359
00:18:18,604 --> 00:18:21,565
I didn't expect him
to take you under his wing.

360
00:18:21,649 --> 00:18:24,735
I thought that, even in a pair,
he'd be out for himself.

361
00:18:25,402 --> 00:18:27,196
The guy that we're talking about...

362
00:18:27,279 --> 00:18:30,407
is Haryu, the one we saw
walking together with Chinatsu?

363
00:18:30,950 --> 00:18:32,034
Then this has gotta mean...

364
00:18:32,827 --> 00:18:35,246
- he wants you to back off his crush.
- [exclaims]

365
00:18:35,329 --> 00:18:36,705
Isn't that kinda the vibe?

366
00:18:37,581 --> 00:18:40,292
- Our worlds are far apart.
- [Hina] <i>Like he's trying to rub your nose</i>

367
00:18:40,376 --> 00:18:42,253
<i>in your difference of status,
so you give up.</i>

368
00:18:43,003 --> 00:18:46,340
[Taiki groans] Well, it's working
'cause I am feeling it.

369
00:18:46,841 --> 00:18:50,761
<i>We do the same training,
but he never slows down.</i>

370
00:18:50,845 --> 00:18:52,596
<i>And his shots are more accurate.</i>

371
00:18:53,848 --> 00:18:58,269
It must be so much more fun to play
when your foundation's that good.

372
00:18:58,853 --> 00:19:00,646
- You nerd.
- Maniac.

373
00:19:00,729 --> 00:19:02,481
[Taiki] Quit it with the insults!

374
00:19:03,607 --> 00:19:05,109
[shuttlecock thudding]

375
00:19:08,112 --> 00:19:09,238
[grunts]

376
00:19:09,321 --> 00:19:12,032
Hey, Taiki. Why'd you do a cross there?

377
00:19:12,783 --> 00:19:14,869
He was in backhand position.

378
00:19:14,952 --> 00:19:17,705
And a straight shot
would've kept the shuttle's speed.

379
00:19:17,788 --> 00:19:20,666
It would've been tougher for you,
but that was the right move.

380
00:19:21,625 --> 00:19:24,670
You're never going to improve
if you only take the easy shot.

381
00:19:24,753 --> 00:19:25,754
Got it!

382
00:19:36,348 --> 00:19:38,601
I survived another day.

383
00:19:38,684 --> 00:19:39,768
Back from battle?

384
00:19:39,852 --> 00:19:42,688
[Taiki] Phew! I would kill for a drink.

385
00:19:42,771 --> 00:19:44,523
[Kyo] Like a soft drink, right?

386
00:19:45,691 --> 00:19:47,276
- Taiki.
- [exclaims]

387
00:19:47,860 --> 00:19:50,154
- Nice hustle.
- [Taiki] Yeah, good practice.

388
00:19:51,322 --> 00:19:54,491
<i>Second-year upperclassmen and Chinatsu.</i>

389
00:19:58,329 --> 00:19:59,163
[chuckles]

390
00:20:03,918 --> 00:20:06,670
So me and this guy got paired up
for doubles this year.

391
00:20:06,754 --> 00:20:07,713
[gasps]

392
00:20:07,796 --> 00:20:10,049
[Taiki] <i>Why is he
talking about me right now?</i>

393
00:20:10,132 --> 00:20:11,425
This kid's a first-year,

394
00:20:11,508 --> 00:20:13,844
and he's just utterly useless.

395
00:20:13,928 --> 00:20:16,180
He has weaknesses everywhere you look.

396
00:20:17,056 --> 00:20:18,515
His control sucks,

397
00:20:18,599 --> 00:20:20,935
and he can get so flustered,
it ruins the play.

398
00:20:21,560 --> 00:20:23,896
[Taiki] <i>It's all true,
so I can't say anything.</i>

399
00:20:23,979 --> 00:20:27,066
But... I think he's gonna be a real force.

400
00:20:27,650 --> 00:20:28,609
[grunts softly]

401
00:20:29,151 --> 00:20:30,694
It doesn't really matter

402
00:20:30,778 --> 00:20:33,572
how much I beat this guy up,
he's never once quit.

403
00:20:34,240 --> 00:20:35,991
Even when I give him extra training

404
00:20:36,075 --> 00:20:38,077
and it seems like
he'd never get through it,

405
00:20:38,160 --> 00:20:40,371
he sticks with it until the very end.

406
00:20:40,454 --> 00:20:41,330
[exclaims]

407
00:20:41,413 --> 00:20:43,165
You are such a tyrant!

408
00:20:43,249 --> 00:20:47,044
Ah, Haryu is hardest on the people
he expects the most from.

409
00:20:47,127 --> 00:20:48,087
[Taiki gasps]

410
00:20:48,170 --> 00:20:50,172
- [Haryu] No, that's not it.
- [Taiki] <i>What a relief.</i>

411
00:20:50,256 --> 00:20:52,174
<i>- He does have some faith in me.</i>
- [boy] It is.

412
00:20:52,258 --> 00:20:54,426
Anybody who's average, you ignore.
Right, Nishida?

413
00:20:54,510 --> 00:20:56,220
- [Nishida] Huh?
- Sorry about him!

414
00:20:56,303 --> 00:20:58,847
- [Chinatsu whispers] That's great to hear.
- You can be a nicer.

415
00:20:58,931 --> 00:21:02,643
[boy] You know, the other day, there was
this first-year I was looking after...

416
00:21:04,436 --> 00:21:07,481
[Taiki] <i>Honestly,
getting noticed by an upperclassmen...</i>

417
00:21:07,564 --> 00:21:09,108
<i>doesn't feel too bad.</i>

418
00:21:10,943 --> 00:21:13,320
Oh, look, I just got a text
from my girlfriend.

419
00:21:13,404 --> 00:21:15,114
[chuckles] What? From your girlfriend?

420
00:21:16,115 --> 00:21:19,285
[exclaims] Wait,
you have a girlfriend, Haryu?

421
00:21:19,868 --> 00:21:22,621
- I do, since last week.
- [Taiki] Last week?

422
00:21:24,290 --> 00:21:26,041
I've liked her for a long time,

423
00:21:26,125 --> 00:21:28,627
but she works
in the entertainment industry.

424
00:21:29,295 --> 00:21:32,881
I was about to give up on her,
but she ended up asking me out.

425
00:21:33,716 --> 00:21:36,302
- [Taiki grunts]
- [Haryu] She's awesome.

426
00:21:36,385 --> 00:21:40,597
She's had this dream since she was little,
and has really been going after it.

427
00:21:42,099 --> 00:21:44,685
Chii, thanks for your help the other day.

428
00:21:44,768 --> 00:21:47,646
It would've been tough
to buy makeup if I'd been by myself.

429
00:21:48,272 --> 00:21:49,273
No problem.

430
00:21:49,982 --> 00:21:53,902
[Taiki] <i>Wait a second.
He knew all of this the whole time?</i>

431
00:21:53,986 --> 00:21:55,195
[amusing music playing]

432
00:21:55,279 --> 00:21:58,407
Seems like getting a girlfriend for you
might be a ways off, champ.

433
00:21:58,490 --> 00:22:00,409
[grunts angrily]

434
00:22:01,076 --> 00:22:03,620
[Taiki] <i>It's none of your business!</i>

435
00:22:05,497 --> 00:22:07,499
[closing theme song playing]
